+++5. run the 1,000-sequence production benchmark.
+++
+++Only then may:
+++
+++```text
+++BACKEND_INTEGRATED = TRUE
+++SUITE_SCOPE = INTEGRATED_PRODUCTION_STACK
+++P0_PRE_READY = TRUE
+++```
+++
+++if all other gates pass.
+++
+++---
+++
+++# C7. Cache invalidation must cover the backend
+++
+++The production cache identity must change whenever executable scoring semantics change.
+++
+++The cache key must include a deterministic code identity covering at least:
+++
+++```text
+++canonical scorer implementation
+++HF/PEFT backend adapter
+++token masking/reduction logic
+++reference-loss implementation
+++Min-K implementation
+++tokenizer revision/config
+++precision
+++max sequence length
+++artifact/model hash
+++record-set hash
+++```
+++
+++A manually typed `scorer_version` string alone is insufficient.
+++
+++Preferred:
+++
+++```text
+++SCORING_CODE_HASH = SHA256(relevant source files + resolved scoring config)
+++```
+++
+++Then include `SCORING_CODE_HASH` in the content-addressed cache key.
+++
+++Negative tests:
+++
+++```text
+++backend source change -> cache miss
+++score reducer change  -> cache miss
+++unchanged code/config -> cache hit + bitwise-identical scalar score table
+++```
+++
+++---
+++
+++# C8. Production scaffold status
+++
+++The existing P0 scaffold is a **reference fixture**, not the production repository.
+++
+++Claude Code must port/reimplement its validated behaviour into the reproducible repo built under `01_EXECUTION_STACK_LOCK_v2.md`.
+++
+++Do not copy code merely because a synthetic fixture passed.
+++
+++Every production component must pass:
+++
+++```text
+++Claude implementation
+++fresh Claude adversarial review
+++Codex independent review where required
+++ChatGPT acceptance
+++```
+++
+++before it becomes evidentiary.
+++
+++---
+++
+++# Final locked interpretation
+++
+++No new scientific question is opened by these corrections.
+++
+++The primary endpoint remains:
+++
+++\[
+++\boxed{\mathrm{TPR}@1\%\mathrm{FPR}}
+++\]
+++
+++at a common held-out evaluation FPR.
+++
+++The corrections ensure that:
+++
+++- ties cannot create impossible ROC points;
+++- finite-sample fixed-FPR bias is measured;
+++- DRY-G controls family-wise false failure rather than marginal false failure;
+++- backend integration cannot be mistaken for completed synthetic-statistics validation;
+++- stale cache cannot survive a backend/code change.
